{
  "spec": "exec protocol v1.4 sandbox job notify (crates/agent/src/exec_endpoint.rs, \"Sandbox job notify (v1.4)\"), \"The callback request\" and \"The receiver\"",
  "notes": [
    "requests: what an endpoint sends for a job kept with notify. body is the exact bytes; headers lists every header the endpoint must send (others the HTTP client adds, such as Host and Content-Length, are not listed, and a Cookie header is forbidden).",
    "receiver: one request to keep.url, which names url_session's tenant and session id. It carries no session grant. request.authorization lists its Authorization header values, in order (empty: none). state is what the replica holds: service_mode, notify_key (it holds the verifier keys of v1.4-token.json), open_here (a session task in this process holds that session for that tenant), job (released: the session tracks it released and the sandbox still runs it; ended_unreported: the sandbox has it ended and the session has not recorded its end; held: the session holds its stream and the callback is not its proof; end_reported: the session has recorded its end; open_reconcile_pending: the session's open reconcile has not run yet; untracked: the session neither tracks the job nor has recorded its end), reconcile (ok, or fails: the sandbox cannot be listed), run_in_flight (a run holds the session). expect: the HTTP status, the response's data.listener on a 200, and whether anything is sent to the sandbox. No case opens a session: a callback never does.",
    "edge: how the edge classifies a request by its Authorization header values (E1, with the rules of N28): callback (forwarded unchanged to the hashed replica), user (handled as any user request), or refused with status, never forwarded."
  ],
  "keep": {
    "scope": "2ff302a37e7401aa95f92ec6c431944a",
    "id": "0123456789abcdef",
    "url": "https://edge.example/_beyond/agent?session_id=a07-s3.01J9ZQ4N6V&tenant=acme&keep=5be0c2a19f3d7e41",
